{
  "world": "/Game/Maps/LVL_CommanderMassPrototype.LVL_CommanderMassPrototype",
  "api": {
    "export_material_graph": "X.export_material_graph(material_path) -> str\r\nExport the complete material graph as a JSON string for analysis or recreation.\nMaps to action=\"export_graph\"\n\nReturns material settings, all expressions (type, position, properties),\nall connections, and material output connections \u2014 everything needed to\nrecreate the material from scratch.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    material_path (str): Full path to the material\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    str: JSON string of complete graph, or empty string on failure Example: json_str = unreal.MaterialNodeService.export_material_graph(\"/Game/M_Landscape\")",
    "connect_expressions": "X.connect_expressions(material_path, source_expression_id, source_output, target_expression_id, target_input) -> bool\r\nConnect two material expressions.\nMaps to action=\"connect\"\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    material_path (str): Full path to the material\r\n    source_expression_id (str): Source expression ID\r\n    source_output (str): Output name (empty for first output)\r\n    target_expression_id (str): Target expression ID\r\n    target_input (str): Input name on target\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool: True if successful",
    "disconnect_output": "X.disconnect_output(material_path, material_property) -> bool\r\nDisconnect a material output property.\nMaps to action=\"disconnect_output\"\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    material_path (str): Full path to the material\r\n    material_property (str): Property name to disconnect\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    bool: True if successful",
    "get_material_diagnostics": "X.get_material_diagnostics(material_path) -> MaterialDiagnostics\r\nComprehensive material diagnostic \u2014 compile status, errors, and the textures the\nshader actually references. Reliable replacement for `get_used_textures`.\n\nUse this after building a material graph to verify it compiles cleanly and samples\nthe expected textures. Particularly useful for materials with `MaterialFunctionCall`\nnodes (triplanar / world-aligned), where `MaterialEditingLibrary.get_used_textures`\nsilently returns 0.\r\n\r\nArgs:\r\n    material_path (str): \r\n\r\nReturns:\r\n    MaterialDiagnostics:"
  },
